Welcome to Zenix, a small Unix-like system for Amigas (68020 or better).

The whole disk now runs from memory: programs start at once, the floppy
may be taken out, and nothing is ever written to it. Your files live in
memory (about 250 KB of room) until the Amiga is switched off.

 Icons, the Zenix menu    a shell, Files (Ahiru), Editor (Sumi),
                          Monitor (ctop), each in a terminal window
 Amiga+Return             a new terminal      Amiga+Q      close a window
 Amiga+Tab                the next window     Amiga+Space  the menu
 Amiga+F2 .. Amiga+F10    text consoles (log in as guest);
                          Amiga+F1 comes back here
 man demo                 what is on this disk (man NAME: each command)
 ifconfig                 the network: a card is set up by DHCP

Press Return to close this window.
